The static part of S9 is built and green on the current tree. The new tests were GREEN on their first run (the F1-F7 fixes are in the tree). I proved each one can go RED, in memory and by real-file mutation on files I may mutate. Two spec items could not be built as written because production code is private or missing: the exact-form /continue preflight case (see blockers) and the sync script --self-test, which cannot run in this worktree.

What I built:
1. execution-core tests/loop_fold_zdr_matrix.rs (7 tests) runs the vendored zdr-posture-matrix.json (27 enforcement rows, split 18 refuse / 4 zdr / 3 persistent / 2 waived) through mp_contracts resolve_turn. It checks:
   - decision and code against the golden;
   - the stored class against the golden vocabulary (zdr to zdr, persistent to persistent, waived to zdr_waived);
   - that refuse_unless_persistent is Ok for all four DurableStore values (Fold, Consume, Continue, Park) exactly on the three persistent rows. A resolver refusal passes through unchanged; Zdr and Waived get zdr_feature_not_supported naming the store's feature;
   - that refuse_unless_persistent_class agrees with the decision gate on every served row;
   - that loop_mode_for_persistent gives loop only for a persistent row with the switch on;
   - two anti-vacuity checks: a hand-built Waived is refused, and the pre-fix "not ZDR" rule must disagree with the matrix on exactly the two waived rows (e_waiver_on_bound_route, e_equal_waived_bearers).
2. execution-core tests/durable_loop_contract.rs (13 tests) reads source with comments stripped and cfg(test) cut out through a small Rust-aware cleaner. Each guard is a pure function over source text, and one test proves each goes red on an in-memory copy broken the way a careless edit would:
   - tool_loop.rs has none of the 13 forbidden resume-path tokens;
   - exactly one /continue route in the gateway, bound to post(crate::sse::continue_run), and exactly one production AgentResume literal, in sse.rs;
   - the gateway builder (continue_resume) and the executor validator (enforce_resume) agree: builder mode "segment" is accepted, the builder sends segment_no 0 exactly once, nobody reads .segment_no, and a non-zero value is not refused;
   - run_agent refuses a zero-retention caller before enforce_resume;
   - the pause site passes not-ZDR AND is_waived() to run_pause_mode, and continuation_mode_for is gone everywhere;
   - the mode words agree across planes (gate mints "" and loop, session-core stores both, the gateway requires loop, the executor accepts loop and refuses empty);
   - the retention-class literal in the CONSUME_APPROVAL_SQL and run_owner_tx SQL is the class refuse_unless_persistent_class opens and the matrix's persistent class;
   - DURABLE_MUTATIONS names ("sse.rs","continue_run");
   - every durable-loop switch is set on the services that read it (model-gateway and execution-core for AGENT_CONTINUE_AFTER_APPROVAL_ENABLED; execution-core for the effect ledger and EXECUTION_LOOP_CHECKPOINT_ENABLED; session-core for the fold store and ledger sweep), names matching the consts in source, default :-false, and every *_ENABLED loop switch in all five compose files defaults false;
   - the continue switch is parsed only through mp-contracts;
   - the fold writer gate (s6's fold::WriterGate) is off for zdr and waived, is fed from ctx.route.is_waived(), and EXECUTION_LOOP_CHECKPOINT_ENABLED uses the strict mp_contracts switch_from.
3. Vendored fixtures: execution-core tests/fixtures/zdr-posture-matrix.json and its .sha256, byte-identical to the canonical copies.
4. scripts/tests/zdr-contract-sync.test.sh gained two VENDORED rows and one CONSUMERS row (execution-core). The script now reports 70 passed, 22 failed. The 22 failures are all pre-existing: missing rerank, retrieve and usage-ledger goldens, a stale cross-plane-token-requests pin, and CRLF .sha256 mismatches. Before my rows it reported 67 passed, 22 failed, so the three new checks pass and the failure set is unchanged.
5. model-gateway tests/zdr_posture_matrix.rs gained 2 tests, written to the repo's CRLF convention:
   - a_continue_is_served_to_a_persistent_bearer_on_every_row_and_to_nothing_else decides every bearer of every row with zdr_posture::decide_for over Route::plain(false), the decision /continue makes. It is served exactly when the bearer is persistent, using an oracle written from the matrix's own rule. It also requires at least 3 served, 2 waived-with-zdr-false refused and 3 zdr refused, and agreement with the row's decision where /continue and the row name the same turn.
   - the_continue_handler_decides_its_turn_with_the_plain_route_and_serves_persistent_only holds that the private continue_turn_is_persistent in sse.rs is exactly decide_for over the plain route returning Persistent only, and that continue_run hands it to the preflight and calls continue_persistent_gate.

Mutation checks (every file restored byte for byte, verified with cmp):
- durable_gate.rs A1 (waived accepted by refuse_unless_persistent): 4 of 7 matrix tests red.
- durable_gate.rs A2 (class gate also opens for zdr_waived): 2 matrix tests plus the contract self-test red.
- durable_gate.rs A3 (loop mode ignores persistent): the minting test red.
- durable_gate.rs A4 (every served decision accepted): 4 matrix tests red.
- sse.rs B1 (segment_no: 2): the builder-and-validator guard and the self-test red.
- sse.rs B2 (/continue serves Waived): the new gateway handler test red.
- Sync script: tampering with or deleting the vendored copy fails the new row.

Pass counts after:
- execution-core: lib 959, durable_loop_contract 13, loop_fold_zdr_matrix 7, scrub 8, and the other integration binaries unchanged.
- model-gateway: lib 1817, e2e 118, zdr_posture_matrix 6 (was 4), and the other binaries unchanged.
- Baseline: I did not capture the lib counts before starting. The baseline run exists but its tail only kept the integration binaries. Counts that moved belong to s6 and s7a (lib, scrub 4 to 8) or to my additions.
